{{<storefront/layout}}
{{$content}}    <h1>{{policy.title}}</h1>
{{!The body is rendered UNESCAPED, deliberately, and it is the most reviewable
    line in this file. It is HTML the operator wrote about their own storefront,
    stored verbatim, and escaping it would print the tags on the page instead of
    applying them. The rule that bans unescaped output is about MERCHANT-AUTHORED
    TEMPLATES, which we do not accept; this is our template rendering their
    content, which is the trust boundary Shopify's own page and policy rendering
    sits on, and pages.body already stores raw HTML for exactly this reason.
    It is still a boundary — MAP records it as the first operator-authored HTML
    rendered raw, so that operator-authored THEMES are visibly a separate
    decision rather than the same one.
    NB a Mustache comment ends at the first close-brace pair, so this one cannot
    quote the tag it is about.}}
    <div>{{{policy.body}}}</div>{{/content}}
{{/storefront/layout}}
